abstract: >-
  E7G-T is a geometry-first modelling language and practical calculus
  for making construction, projection, preservation, loss,
  reconstruction, operational sameness, material boundaries,
  temporal extension, histories, transition paths, bridge mode,
  and admissible use visible.
  UC2 additionally provides an informative pilot module for separating
  observational claims from interpretations and composing observer-indexed
  observational fields while preserving disagreement, unknowns, and temporal limits.
  UC3 additionally provides an informative temporal-orientation module that separates
  reverse reconstruction from time-reversal symmetry and causal reversal, distinguishes
  history-whole membership from simultaneity, and models observer-relative history relevance.
  UC4 additionally provides an informative topological-overlay module that separates
  operational adjacency and phase boundaries from topological notions, supports declared
  quotient topologies, and keeps topology distinct from metric, order, orientation, and causation.
